"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2023-01-01:0":{"b": ["Susa: Ur III (Third Dynasty of Ur) → Elam — Shimashki Dynasty", "565be22a"], "d": ["At the points Susa, ownership passes from Ur III (Third Dynasty of Ur) to the Elam — Shimashki Dynasty. Transition source information: disintegration of Ur III: in Ibbi-Suen year 3 (MC 2024) the eastern/northern provinces (Eshnunna, Susa) break away | Source: Sallaberger, W. & Schrakamp, I. (eds.) 2015, ARCANE III: History & Philology, Brepols (Kisim I; Middle Chronology=MC), p. 131 | http://www.assyriologie.uni-muenchen.de/personen/professoren/sallaberger/publ_sallaberger/wasa_schrakamp_2015_arcane1.pdf | «in Ibbisuen year 3 (MC 2024) provinces in the east and north, including Eshnuna and Susa»", "ec232f42"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2024-01-01:0":{"b": ["Uruk, Ur: Ur III (Third Dynasty of Ur) → Kingdom of Larsa", "13e410be"], "d": ["At the points Uruk, Ur, ownership passes from Ur III (Third Dynasty of Ur) to the Kingdom of Larsa. Transition source information: 16th century BCE: Babylonia is divided in two - the Kassites in the north, the Sealand in the south including Uruk, Ur and Larsa | Source: Zadok, R., \"Kassites\", Encyclopaedia Iranica XVI/2, 2013, pp. 113-118 (rev. 2015); chronology Boese 1982 / Brinkman 1986 | https://web.archive.org/web/2025/https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/kassites | «Babylonia was divided into two kingdoms, that of the Kassites in the north and the Sealand in the south, including Uruk, Ur, and Larsa»", "60b4e47e"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2111-01-01:0":{"b": ["Uruk: Gutium (Gutian) Rule → ownerless interval", "215ec8a9"], "d": ["At the points Uruk, ownership passes from Gutium (Gutian) Rule to the ownerless interval. Transition source information: Uruk breaks away from the Akkad state: in the late years of Sharkalisharri (MC 2205-2181) or a little later | Source: Sallaberger, W. & Schrakamp, I. (eds.) 2015, ARCANE III: History & Philology, Brepols (Kisim I; Middle Chronology=MC), p. 117 | http://www.assyriologie.uni-muenchen.de/personen/professoren/sallaberger/publ_sallaberger/wasa_schrakamp_2015_arcane1.pdf | «Uruk left the state of Akkad before Girsu, i.e. probably in the late years of Sharkalisharri, or slightly later»", "4300e5fb"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2143-01-01:0":{"b": ["Girsu (center of the Lagash state): ownerless interval → Lagash II Period (Ur-Baba, Gudea, Ur-Ningirsu)", "76d5858c"], "d": ["At the points Girsu (center of the Lagash state), ownership passes from the ownerless interval to the Lagash II Period (Ur-Baba, Gudea, Ur-Ningirsu). Transition source information: independence of Girsu/Lagash from Akkad: Puzurmama is the first independent ruler; \"period of confusion\" (after Sharkalisharri, MC 2181-2177) | Source: Sallaberger, W. & Schrakamp, I. (eds.) 2015, ARCANE III: History & Philology, Brepols (Kisim I; Middle Chronology=MC), p. 119 | http://www.assyriologie.uni-muenchen.de/personen/professoren/sallaberger/publ_sallaberger/wasa_schrakamp_2015_arcane1.pdf | «It is possible to date the beginning of independence to the period of confusion»", "8d39c3f8"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2153-01-01:0":{"b": ["Uruk: ownerless interval → Gutium (Gutian) Rule", "30cdee11"], "d": ["At the points Uruk, ownership passes from the ownerless interval to Gutium (Gutian) Rule. Transition source information: Uruk breaks away from the Akkad state: in the late years of Sharkalisharri (MC 2205-2181) or a little later | Source: Sallaberger, W. & Schrakamp, I. (eds.) 2015, ARCANE III: History & Philology, Brepols (Kisim I; Middle Chronology=MC), p. 117 | http://www.assyriologie.uni-muenchen.de/personen/professoren/sallaberger/publ_sallaberger/wasa_schrakamp_2015_arcane1.pdf | «Uruk left the state of Akkad before Girsu, i.e. probably in the late years of Sharkalisharri, or slightly later»", "f824d29b"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2153-01-01:1":{"b": ["Kish, Ur: Akkadian Empire period ends", "dac43da0"], "d": ["In the s: sequence of the points Kish, Ur, this boundary comes from the f/t limit of the owner entity (Akkadian Empire) or from the kur:/bit: end of the point; the entity sources are in data/devletler.js. It is NOT a separate historical event but a period-end record (Invariant 2).", "026a8e96"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2294-01-01:0":{"b": ["Mari: City Kingdom of Mari (Mari II, Early Dynastic-Akkadian) period ends", "77cd219c"], "d": ["In the s: sequence of the points Mari, this boundary comes from the f/t limit of the owner entity (City Kingdom of Mari (Mari II, Early Dynastic-Akkadian)) or from the kur:/bit: end of the point; the entity sources are in data/devletler.js. It is NOT a separate historical event but a period-end record (Invariant 2).", "e713f896"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2299-01-01:0":{"b": ["Umma, Ur: ownerless interval → Akkadian Empire", "25980168"], "d": ["At the points Umma, Ur, ownership passes from the ownerless interval to the Akkadian Empire. Transition source information: Sargon defeats Lugalzagesi; Akkadian rule begins in the south of Babylonia (Table 39: \"Sargonic period beginning in Babylonia\" ca. 2300, MC; MC II ca. 2292) | Source: Sallaberger, W. & Schrakamp, I. (eds.) 2015, ARCANE III: History & Philology, Brepols (Kisim I; Middle Chronology=MC), p. 90; Table 39 p. 136 | http://www.assyriologie.uni-muenchen.de/personen/professoren/sallaberger/publ_sallaberger/wasa_schrakamp_2015_arcane1.pdf | «he defeated Lugalzagesi of Uruk and thus became the only king of ", "c017226e"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2299-01-01:1":{"b": ["Eridu, Ur: ownerless interval ends", "65f8717f"], "d": ["In the s: sequence of the points Eridu, Ur, this boundary comes from the f/t limit of the owner entity (ownerless interval) or from the kur:/bit: end of the point; the entity sources are in data/devletler.js. It is NOT a separate historical event but a period-end record (Invariant 2).", "f6547741"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2309-01-01:0":{"b": ["Ebla: First Kingdom of Ebla period ends", "c328fc97"], "d": ["In the s: sequence of the points Ebla, this boundary comes from the f/t limit of the owner entity (First Kingdom of Ebla) or from the kur:/bit: end of the point; the entity sources are in data/devletler.js. It is NOT a separate historical event but a period-end record (Invariant 2).", "1242c7e5"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2323-01-01:0":{"b": ["Eridu, Umma, Uruk, Ur: ownerless interval begins", "6f8b2cb5"], "d": ["In the s: sequence of the points Eridu, Umma, Uruk, Ur, this boundary comes from the f/t limit of the owner entity (ownerless interval) or from the kur:/bit: end of the point; the entity sources are in data/devletler.js. It is NOT a separate historical event but a period-end record (Invariant 2).", "ffc56ba6"]},
"OLAYLAR_ARKEOLOJI_ZINCIR:-2349-01-01:0":{"b": ["Girsu (center of the Lagash state): First Dynasty of Lagash (city-state) → ownerless interval", "92acbeca"], "d": ["At the points Girsu (center of the Lagash state), ownership passes from the First Dynasty of Lagash (city-state) to the ownerless interval. Transition source information: Urnanshe (Lagash I) marks the beginning of the Presargonic period; from Urnanshe year 1 to Lugalzagesi year 25 about 175 years (lower estimate); Table 39: ca. 2475-2300±30 (MC) | Source: Sallaberger, W. & Schrakamp, I. (eds.) 2015, ARCANE III: History & Philology, Brepols (Kisim I; Middle Chronology=MC), pp. 67, 84; Table 39 p. 136 | http://www.assyriologie.uni-muenchen.de/personen/professoren/sallaberger/publ_sallaberger/wasa_schrakamp_2015_arcane1.pdf | «The reign of Urnanshe marks the beginning of the Presargonic period»", "835348be"]},
